# Mind Framework Environment Template
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in any secrets your domain
# integrations need. Format: KEY=value (no quotes for simple values;
# quote strings with spaces).
#
# The framework itself does NOT require any environment variables to
# operate. Add credentials below as needed by your forged skills (e.g.,
# API keys for external services, SSH paths for remote filesystems,
# cloud credentials).
#
# SECURITY:
#   - .env.local is gitignored by default. Do NOT commit secrets.
#   - If you do commit secrets to .env.local by accident, rotate them
#     before pushing to any remote.
#   - For team deployments, consider a secrets manager (Vault, AWS
#     Secrets Manager, etc.) instead of plaintext .env.local files.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional placeholders — uncomment and fill in as needed for your domain
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# API keys for external services your domain integrates with
# MY_SERVICE_API_KEY=
# MY_SERVICE_URL=

# Credentials for remote filesystems
# MY_REMOTE_HOST=
# MY_SSH_KEY_PATH=

# Cloud credentials (rotate before committing anywhere public!)
# CLOUD_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# CLOUD_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# CLOUD_REGION=

# Notification destinations
# USER_EMAIL=
# TEAM_NOTIFY_EMAIL=
